license:        BSD-3-Clause
vendored:       2026-06-03
files:          zsh-syntax-highlighting.zsh + highlighters/{main,brackets,pattern,cursor,line,regexp,root}/
                dot_version + dot_revision-hash (deploy as .version / .revision-hash → populate
                $ZSH_HIGHLIGHT_VERSION / _REVISION). The entry reads BOTH at load (no 2>/dev/null on
                the .revision-hash read), so a missing .revision-hash prints to stderr every startup —
                keep both vendored.
note:           Leading-dot .vendor → chezmoi-ignored; provenance only, never deployed.
                Entry uses ${0:A:h} to find highlighters/ — keep the tree intact.
                Bump: re-download the new tag tarball, replace files (incl. dot_version +
                dot_revision-hash from upstream .version / .revision-hash), refresh tag + tarball
                sha256 here.
